-- Space reductions, the non-uniform field (ex30). Twin of 30-space-reductions.bqn (the 3 3 cost2 half).
-- The same two scans on a field small enough to check by hand: 3x3, costs 1..9. The one-axis scan and the summed-area table disagree everywhere past the first row, which is the point.
-- The same Version A / Version B scan pair on the 3 3 field 1..9 — the .bqn's cost2, registered here as cost so the canonical statement reads unchanged. Every cell hand-computed: one-axis rows 1 2 3 / 5 7 9 / 12 15 18, SAT 1 3 6 / 5 12 21 / 12 27 45.
-- The explicit (+`cost2) ≢ +`˘+`cost2 witness is carried by the two differing out lines.
--! registry ../registries/30-space-reductions-b.reg
--! out 1 2 3 5 7 9 12 15 18
--! out 1 3 6 5 12 21 12 27 45

+\ Cost @ 3 3                        -- Version A: leading-axis scan
scan2(+) Cost @ 3 3                  -- Version B: summed-area table
